Date: Thu, 05 Apr 2012 02:16:51 +0000
Subject: Making the line width of points proportional to its size
Message-ID: <c78MAUwLXnI.vgeRTUptRZMJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/c78MAUwLXnI/m/vgeRTUptRZMJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear list members,

An year ago I copied the code below from an email to this mailing list (which I apologize for not being able to find) and I being using it successfully to make the line-width of geom_point of shape=1 proportional to its size (this is because to me it seems it is too thick, and I prefer almost all lines in a plot to have the same width). The variable to look into is "width". This worked fine for ggplot2 0.8.9 but when trying to use it in the new 0.9.0 version it gives me the following error: "object 'GeomPoint' not found".

############################################################
GeomPoint$draw <- function (., data, scales, coordinates, na.rm = FALSE, ...)
{
  data <- remove_missing(data, na.rm, c("x", "y", "size", "width", "shape"),
                         name = "geom_point")
  if (empty(data))
    return(zeroGrob())
  with(coordinates$transform(data, scales), ggname(.$my_name(),
                                                   pointsGrob(x, y, size = unit(size, "mm"), pch = shape,
                                                              gp = gpar(col = alpha(colour, alpha), fill = fill,
                                                                fontsize = size * ggplot2:::.pt, lex = width))))

}

GeomPoint$default_aes <-  function (.)
  aes(shape = 16, colour = "black", size = 1.5, fill = NA, alpha = 1,
      width = 0.6)

GeomPoint$draw_legend <- function (., data, ...)
{
  if (!is.null(data$fill) && !all(is.na <http://is.na>(data$fill)) && data$shape ==
      16) {
    data$shape <- 21
  }
  data <- aesdefaults(data, .$default_aes(), list(...))
  with(data, pointsGrob(0.5, 0.5, size = unit(size, "mm"),
                        pch = shape, gp = gpar(col = alpha(colour, alpha), fill = alpha(fill,
                                                                             alpha), fontsize = size * .pt, lex = width)))
}
############################################################

Is it possible to do the same for ggplot 0.9.0? I think that the function to change is not coming from "GeomPoint" any more but from "geom_grob.point", as in the code below:

geom_grob.point <- function(geom, data) {
  gp <- gpar(col = alpha(data$colour, data$alpha), fill = data$fill,
    fontsize = data$size * .pt)
  pointsGrob(data$x, data$y, size = unit(data$size, "mm"), pch = data$shape,
    gp = data$gp)
}

Thanks for your help,

Alan

