There may be other issues, but one is that ggplot2 0.9 depends on  R
(>= 2.14).  2.15.0 has already been released, so I would suggest
updating.  There are loads of nice new features in R and ggplot2.

After that, you should just be able to do:

install.packages("ggplot2", repos = "your favorite repo")

rather than building it yourself (which it looks like ??? you were
trying to do).

Cheers,

Josh

